{#- Rendered from commit_types in copier.yml plus the labels the workflows
    name. GitHub's own defaults (bug, enhancement, documentation, question and
    the rest) exist on every repository and are left alone; the stale label is
    created by the action that applies it; labels-sync does not delete what
    this file does not list. The release drafter's autolabeler applies a type
    label from the pull request title, and that one label is what files the
    pull request under a heading: a labeler that added docs, ci and
    dependencies from the changed paths put one pull request under three
    headings of the same draft. -#}
# Rendered by copier from the commit types in copier.yml, which the release
# drafter and its autolabeler read as well.
{%- for t in commit_types %}
- name: "{{ t.type }}"
  color: "{{ t.color }}"
  description: "Conventional Commits type: {{ t.type }}"
{%- endfor %}
- name: "breaking"
  color: "b60205"
  description: "Breaking change; a major bump"
- name: "dependencies"
  color: "0366d6"
  description: "Dependency update"
- name: "security"
  color: "ee0701"
  description: "Security-related"
- name: "skip-changelog"
  color: "ededed"
  description: "Left out of the release notes"
- name: "pinned"
  color: "0052cc"
  description: "Exempt from the stale bot"
- name: "blocked"
  color: "b60205"
  description: "Blocked on a dependency or a decision; exempt from the stale bot"
- name: "work-in-progress"
  color: "fbca04"
  description: "Not ready for review; exempt from the stale bot"
